diagnosis_text:
The failure is in the routing control plane, not the host cabling. pc_0_0’s ping to 10.0.1.2 returns “Destination Net Unreachable” from 10.0.0.1, proving leaf_router_0_0 (pc_0_0’s gateway) lacks a route to 10.0.1.0/24. On leaf_router_0_0, BGP is up to both spines but it receives 0 prefixes, so it cannot learn 10.0.1.0/24. The spines each show their BGP neighbor to leaf_router_0_1 in Active (down) state, and super_spine only carries one prefix (10.0.0.0/24) from the fabric. Critically, on leaf_router_0_1, “bgpd is not running” and systemd reports frr.service is failed. Although leaf_router_0_1 has 10.0.1.0/24 as a connected route (interface eth2 up), its BGP process is down, so that prefix is never advertised
